| Intentional element identified (literal excerpt)                                                                      | Class    | Justification                                                                                                                                                              |
| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| “deliver food from the kitchen to an inpatient room”                                                                  | Goal     | This states a desired system state or outcome: food is delivered to the inpatient room. It does not, by itself, fully prescribe how delivery must be performed.            |
| “The delivery is made on an order-by-order basis in response to kitchen delivery requests”                            | Task     | This specifies a particular operational way of performing food delivery: each delivery is triggered by a kitchen request and handled order by order.                       |
| “kitchen delivery requests”                                                                                           | Resource | This is an informational entity required to initiate delivery. The concern is whether such requests are available to the robot/system.                                     |
| “The food can be delivered into a room table by the robot”                                                            | Task     | This is a specific alternative way of achieving food delivery: the robot places the food on the room table.                                                                |
| “requires a special manipulation robot skill”                                                                         | Resource | The manipulation skill is an available capability needed for the robot to perform table delivery.                                                                          |
| “the food can be fetched from the robot's tray”                                                                       | Task     | This is another specific alternative way of achieving delivery: someone retrieves the food from the robot tray.                                                            |
| “Fetching from the robot tray requires cooperation with the inpatient, a companion, a nurse, or another robot”        | Belief   | This expresses domain rationale about the conditions under which tray fetching can work: cooperation from some actor is required.                                          |
| “cooperation with the inpatient, a companion, a nurse, or another robot”                                              | Resource | Cooperation is a required availability-dependent entity/capability for completing tray-based delivery.                                                                     |
| “Some inpatients could be unable to fetch the food from the tray”                                                     | Belief   | This is domain knowledge that affects design decisions, explaining why tray fetching may not always be feasible.                                                           |
| “a companion visitor or nurse could not be available at the moment of the delivery”                                   | Belief   | This captures a domain constraint/rationale about possible unavailability of human collaborators.                                                                          |
| “a companion visitor or nurse”                                                                                        | Resource | These are human resources whose availability matters for assisted food retrieval.                                                                                          |
| “The information about if the inpatient, a companion visitor or nurse can be able to retrieve the food from the tray” | Resource | This is informational content needed for deciding whether tray retrieval is feasible.                                                                                      |
| **“can be obtained based on the inpatient record”**                                                                   | **Task** | **This specifies a concrete way of obtaining the information needed to determine whether tray-based food retrieval is feasible.**                                          |
| “the inpatient record”                                                                                                | Resource | This is an informational resource used to determine whether food can be retrieved from the tray.                                                                           |
| “information about the patient”                                                                                       | Resource | This is informational input needed to assess whether the inpatient can retrieve food.                                                                                      |
| “the presence of a companion into the room”                                                                           | Resource | This is availability-related information needed to determine whether tray retrieval can be assisted.                                                                       |
| “This information is subject to uncertainty”                                                                          | Softgoal | Managing or tolerating uncertainty is a quality concern without a clear-cut satisfaction criterion; it affects how confidently the system can decide on a delivery method. |
| “The robot can carry multiple meals”                                                                                  | Belief   | This describes a domain/system capability that motivates the need to identify the correct meal for each inpatient.                                                         |
| “multiple meals”                                                                                                      | Resource | Meals are physical entities carried and delivered by the robot; their identity and availability matter for correct delivery.                                               |
| “the robot should indicate which meal should be retrieved by a given inpatient”                                       | Goal     | This states a functional requirement the system should achieve: make clear which meal corresponds to which inpatient.                                                      |
| “a given inpatient”                                                                                                   | Resource | The inpatient identity is required to associate a particular meal with its intended recipient.                                                                             |
| “track when and where each meal was retrieved”                                                                        | Goal     | This states a desired system capability: recording the time and location of each meal retrieval.                                                                           |
| “when and where each meal was retrieved”                                                                              | Resource | This represents informational data that must be captured and made available for meal traceability.                                                                         |
| “The robot should alert if a wrong meal is retrieved”                                                                 | Goal     | This defines a required system outcome: detection and alerting when an incorrect meal is taken.                                                                            |
| “Dirty dishes should be retrieved from the room”                                                                      | Goal     | This states a desired state of affairs: dirty dishes are removed from the inpatient room.                                                                                  |
| “the dish retrieve can occur unassisted”                                                                              | Task     | This is a specific way of achieving dirty-dish retrieval without cooperation from others.                                                                                  |
| “with the cooperation of two robots”                                                                                  | Task     | This is a specific alternative method for retrieving dishes using two robots.                                                                                              |
| “with the cooperation of robots and a human”                                                                          | Task     | This is another specific alternative method for retrieving dishes involving both robots and a person.                                                                      |
| “Opening the room door”                                                                                               | Goal     | Door opening is a desired enabling condition for food delivery or dish retrieval and can be achieved through different methods.                                            |
| “Opening the room door can involve cooperation with another robot or a human”                                         | Task     | This specifies possible operational ways to accomplish door opening through cooperation.                                                                                   |
| “another robot or a human”                                                                                            | Resource | These are resources whose availability may be required to open the room door.                                                                                              |
| “Someone in the room can call a robot to pick up the dishes”                                                          | Task     | This describes a specific operational process for initiating dish pickup: a person calls the robot.                                                                        |
| “Someone in the room”                                                                                                 | Resource | This person is a possible initiator of dish pickup and may also provide assistance with opening the door.                                                                  |
| “call a robot to pick up the dishes”                                                                                  | Goal     | This expresses the intended outcome of the call: a robot is requested so that dish pickup can occur.                                                                       |
| “that person can signal if they can open the door when the robot comes to it”                                         | Task     | This specifies a concrete interaction mechanism: the person communicates whether they can assist with door opening.                                                        |
| “if they can open the door”                                                                                           | Resource | This is information about the person's availability or capability to assist the robot with opening the door.                                                               |

